Legacy outer-integral regression suites

1 - constant Im, Re = 0
2 - linear Im, Re = 0
3 - constant Im and Re
4 - linear Im and Re
5 - small constant Im, linear Re
21 - small Im = -0.01
22 - small Im = -0.001

The optional suffix selects another reference table while retaining the base
self-energy files. For example, `./run_tests 22 b` reads
`reference_data_22b.dat`, `resigma_22.dat`, and `imsigma_22.dat`.

The suite 5 and 22* references were independently regenerated at 70-100
decimal digits for the exact finite-cutoff command used by `run_tests`. The
energy integral used epsilon = x + gamma tan(theta), and the outer integral was
performed over omega/T in [-15,15]. Exact Hilbert-transform evaluations and
independent quadrature agreed on the nonzero values; all parity-forced zeros
remain exact.

Pointwise clean-limit tests are in `clean_kernel_references.dat`. Their optional
100-decimal-digit mpmath generator is `generate_clean_kernel_references.py`.
